==Finnish==

===Etymology 1===
Either from the pronominal stem ''e-'' seen in {{m|fi|että}} (compare {{m|fi|mikäli}}, from {{m|fi|mikä}}), or alternatively a North Germanic loan (compare {{cog|non|ella}}, {{m|non|ellar}}, from {{cog|gem-pro|*aljaz}}). Also compare {{cog|et|elik}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{fi-pronunciation|(*)}}

====Conjunction====
{{fi-con}}
{{tlb|fi|coordinating}}

# [[that is]], [[that is to say]], [[i.e.]]; [[in other words]], [[to put it another way]]; [[as in]] {{gloss|used to introduce a clarification or explanation}}
#: {{uxi|fi|Hän tulee tänne maanantaina '''eli''' ylihuomenna.|She's coming here on Monday '''as in''' two days from now.}}
#: {{uxi|fi|Kuivajää sublimoituu lämmetessään kaasuksi, '''eli''' se muuttuu suoraan kaasuksi muuttumatta välillä nesteeksi.|Dry ice sublimates to gas directly, '''i.e.''' it turns straight into gas without turning into a liquid in between.}}
# [[or]], [[also known as]], [[AKA]], [[a.k.a.]] {{gloss|used to introduce an alternative name}}
#: {{syn|fi|l.|alias|a.k.a.}}
#: {{uxi|fi|Kikka '''eli''' Kirsi Sirén|Kikka '''a.k.a.''' Kirsi Sirén}}
#: {{uxi|fi|ruokasuola '''eli''' natriumkloridi|table salt '''or''' sodium chloride}}
# {{lb|fi|informal}} [[so]] {{gloss|used to connect previous conversation or events to the following question; used to introduce a rhetorical question}}
#: {{syn|fi|siis|qq1=when not colloquial, it is usually not the first word in the sentence}}
#: {{uxi|fi|'''Eli''' miten se tarina päättyy?|'''So''' how does the story end?}}
#: {{uxi|fi|'''Eli''' kävit siellä eilen.|'''So''' you did go there yesterday.}}
# {{lb|fi|archaic|or|dialectal}} [[or]]
#: {{syn|fi|tai|vai<q:exclusive or in questions>}}
#: {{uxi|fi|Lähdetkö mukaan '''eli''' et?|Are you coming along '''or''' not?}}

